{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`. Tests cover each channel the requirement names (tool results, tool errors, prompts), both exceptions, and the selector-based location rule. I worked from the requirement text and read implementation source only to see which outputs exist.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. No tool result states a line number or range of a project source, except inside quoted source text.\n2. No tool error states one, except where it repeats a number the model supplied.\n3. No prompt states one.\n4. Source locations are identified by file and outline selector, per `requirements.references.outline_selectors`.\n\n**Tool results**\n- `habeas` reads: `reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms` asserts that an item read has no start or end line fields, and that the selector is `fn[work]`. It makes the same assertion for the end-of-file read and checks the recorded input equals the selector-only `outline_input`.\n- Line-range reads: `line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes` asserts that every input in a line-range result has no line fields. It also asserts that results use selectors, including `line@…` selectors for plain text, and that the recorded input carries no line fields.\n- `ripgrep` and `ast_grep`:\n  - `search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules` asserts that entries and their lines have no line-number fields.\n  - `separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line` asserts the exact entry shape of file, item, kind, tag and lines (text and matched only).\n  - Both go through `SearchNodes::entries`, the only output path for search entries.\n- `outline`: `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` asserts the exact JSON for a Rust file, and checks that plain-text entries have no line-start field.\n- `references`: `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` asserts exact equality of the whole result. It contains only name, role, file and item selector, with a null item for a whole file.\n\n**Tool errors**\n- Parse errors: `tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply` runs the real `dispatch` path. A past-the-end read keeps the model-supplied start line it asked for. A real parse error is shown to carry a \"line N:\" position in the raw error. The conversation request delivered to the model contains \"cannot parse\" but no such position.\n- Unit coverage: `tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error` checks `without_source_lines` against these cases.\n  - The Rust parse-error position form.\n  - Both model-supplied forms, a single number and a range, which are preserved unchanged.\n  - The file-prefixed diagnostic form.\n  - A duplicate-declaration message that names a second location.\n  - The YAML and TOML \"at line N, column M\" forms.\n\n**Prompts**\n- `site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site` asserts the exact subject message built from the site file, the selector and the `matches` JSON. That JSON carries kind, query and item only.\n- `sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them` asserts that `matches_value()` for a violation has only kind, query, item and text, with no lines, even though the site holds line fields internally.\n- `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` asserts the exact mandatory inputs, which carry file, item, hash, kind and text only.\n- `submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion` asserts that the submission tool descriptions tell the model to cite \"outline selectors\" and \"never line numbers\".\n- The outline tool description and the habeas tool description state that results carry no line numbers. These are reached through the marked tests above.\n\n**Exceptions**\n- Source text is quoted verbatim in `text` fields, which the requirement permits.\n- A model-supplied number repeated in an error is tested positively and negatively, as described above.\n\n**Residual observations (not gaps)**\n- Parse-error formats for other languages are not each unit-tested. They all go through the same `without_source_lines` call in `HabeasConversation::dispatch`, and the formats the harness produces are covered.\n- The `ast_grep` output path has no dedicated no-line test. It shares the entry builder with `ripgrep`.\n\nNo `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
